        "type": {
          "value": "natural",
          "baseItem": ""
        },
        "description": {
          "value": "<p><em>Melee Weapon Attack:</em> +10, reach 5 ft. <em>Hit:</em> 18 (2d12 + 5) Piercing damage, and the target suffers an additional elemental effect of the dragon's choice:</p><ul><li><strong>Wood.</strong> The target is Poisoned until the end of its next turn. While Poisoned in this way, the target is one size larger and the reach of its melee attacks is increased by 5 feet.</li><li><strong>Fire.</strong> The target is Burning. A creature other than the dragon that comes within 5 feet of the target for the first time on a turn while it's burning in this way takes 2 (1d4) Fire damage.</li><li><strong>Earth.</strong> The target falls Prone. Until the end of its next turn, the target can't right itself from Prone and has Tremorsense with a range of 60 feet.</li><li><strong>Metal.</strong> Until the end of the target's next turn, its weight is tripled, its Speed is halved, it gains a +2 bonus to AC, and it has Disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws.</li><li><strong>Water.</strong> Until the end of the target's next turn, it can't regain Hit Points, and its attacks sap away its own life. When one of the target's weapon attacks against a creature would deal damage, the attacked creature regains that many Hit Points instead, and the attacker takes half that much Necrotic damage.</li></ul>",
          "chat": ""
        },
